  "markdown": {
    "instructions": [
      "SolvaPay quick facts:",
      "- REST API base URL: https://api.solvapay.com. All public endpoints are under /v1/sdk/ (for example GET https://api.solvapay.com/v1/sdk/products). Sandbox and production share this URL.",
      "- Auth: send a secret key as `Authorization: Bearer <secret key>` (the REST API also accepts `X-API-Key: <secret key>`).",
      "- Secret key prefixes: `sk_sandbox_` (sandbox, test payments) and `sk_live_` (production). The prefix selects the environment.",
      "- Get keys in SolvaPay Console (https://app.solvapay.com) > Developers > API Keys. Use a sandbox key while building.",
      "- Admin MCP Server: https://mcp.solvapay.com/mcp (Streamable HTTP). Connect with OAuth: add the URL and sign in with the SolvaPay account; no API key needed. OAuth sessions use the live account; for sandbox data or headless clients, send `Authorization: Bearer <secret key>` (X-API-Key is ignored).",
      "- Install the SolvaPay agent skills: `npx skills add https://solvapay.com` (skills CLI older than 1.5.7: `npx skills add solvapay/skills`).",
      "- TypeScript SDK setup: `npx solvapay@latest init`. The SDK reads SOLVAPAY_SECRET_KEY and defaults to https://api.solvapay.com.",
      "- Plans take an options[] array (billingCycle, charge, limit, ...). Retired plan fields price, freeUnits and billingCycle are rejected.",
      "- Step-by-step from zero to a first paid call: Managed MCP https://docs.solvapay.com/build/managed-mcp.md, TypeScript SDK https://docs.solvapay.com/build/typescript-sdk.md, agent skill https://docs.solvapay.com/build/agent-skill.md.",
      "- Details: https://docs.solvapay.com/api-reference/authentication.md. OpenAPI spec: https://docs.solvapay.com/api-reference/openapi.json."
    ]
  },
